/111432","id":3386086508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J05Rs","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T14:16:31Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T14:16:31Z","body":"> It's a little more complicated than this because x11 includes a file that actually has an absolute path (\"#thirdparty/glad/glx.c\")\r\n\r\nOoooh aight that's fair then. Nw if accounting for it is a mess, it's fine if we append `base` manually too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3386086508/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3386216247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111432#issuecomment-3386216247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111432","id":3386216247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J1Y83","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T14:59:52Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T14:59:52Z","body":"Hi, I've taken a look at the SCons docs and it looks like we might also use a [`File`](https://scons.org/doc/production/HTML/scons-user.html#f-File) node. From what I can tell, it resolves the path on initialization and then can be used anywhere, so that we don't have to hardcode the platform's path.\r\n\r\n> File Nodes can be used anywhere you would supply a string as a file name to a Builder method or function.\r\n\r\nSeems quite handy, let me know if that does the job :D","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3386216247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3386319968","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111432#issuecomment-3386319968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111432","id":3386319968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J1yRg","user":{"login":"zorbathu